{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Motor Control.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Motor Control.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"motor control motor control","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Motor Control.md","fileName":"Motor Control.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Motor Control","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 13:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Human Cognition]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Human Cognition","Feedback","Latency","Fitts's Law","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Motor Control.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Motor Control.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"motor control motor control","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Motor Control.md","fileName":"Motor Control.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Motor Control","heading":"Motor Control","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Motor control governs the selection and execution of physical responses. Open-loop control follows an internal movement plan, while closed-loop control uses sensory [[Feedback]] to make corrections during the movement.\n\nPerformance depends on stimulus-response compatibility, device [[Latency]], visual feedback, coordination, and the tradeoff between speed and accuracy. Aimed movement often has a fast ballistic phase toward a target followed by a corrective phase that brings the motion onto the target.\n\n[[Fitts's Law]] models how target distance and size affect the time required for this kind of movement.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Human Cognition","Feedback","Latency","Fitts's Law","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Motor Control.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Motor Control.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"motor control motor control","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Motor Control.md","fileName":"Motor Control.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Motor Control","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Human Cognition","Feedback","Latency","Fitts's Law","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}